## Android signing

The generator stores the upload keystore and its credentials in AWS Secrets Manager.
Before a local release build, retrieve them into temporary files, create
`android/key.properties`, run `flutter build appbundle`, then delete the temporary files.
The signed bundle is created at `build/app/outputs/bundle/release/app.aab`.

## CI/CD Pipeline (AWS CodePipeline)

This project includes an automated pipeline to build the signed AAB on every push.

### Pipeline components

- **Source:** GitHub repository (webhook on push to main branch)
- **Build:** AWS CodeBuild with Flutter SDK
- **Artifact:** Signed AAB stored in S3

### Required AWS permissions

The CodeBuild IAM role needs access to:

```
secretsmanager:GetSecretValue
Resource: arn:aws:secretsmanager:{region}:{account}:secret:/epc/{applicationId}/android-signing/*
```

### Required variables

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `APPLICATION_ID` | Application identifier (e.g., `com.quizsmart.app`) |
| `AWS_REGION` | AWS region for Secrets Manager |

### Setup

1. Deploy the CloudFormation template: `aws cloudformation deploy --template-file codepipeline.yml --stack-name {app}-pipeline --parameter-overrides GitHubOwner={owner} GitHubRepo={repo} GitHubToken={token}`
2. The pipeline triggers automatically on push to the main branch.
3. The signed AAB is available as a build artifact in the pipeline.

### Local build

```bash
# Retrieve secrets from AWS Secrets Manager
SECRET_PREFIX="/epc/{applicationId}/android-signing"
aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id "$SECRET_PREFIX/keystore" --query SecretBinary --output text | base64 --decode > android/upload-keystore.jks
# Create android/key.properties with storePassword, keyPassword, keyAlias, storeFile
flutter build appbundle --release
# Clean up
rm -f android/key.properties android/upload-keystore.jks
```
